  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_13' aria-label=\" ITC Limited versus Aashna Roy pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('13','2026','2026_2_455_480','2026INSC135'); ><font size='4'> <strong>ITC LIMITED<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>AASHNA ROY </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 2 S.C.R. 455</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 135</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000512026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : RAJESH BINDAL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, MANMOHAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose whether the National Commission was justified in awarding a compensation of \u20b92 crores to the respondent-model for a faulty haircut she took at the beauty salon in the appellant&rsquo;s Hotel. Headnotes&dagger; Consumer Protection Act, 1986 &ndash; Deficiency the beauty salon in the appellant&rsquo;s hotel for haircut &ndash; Dissatisfied with the services rendered, she filed complaint before National Commission &ndash; Commission awarded a compensation of \u20b92 crores to the respondent holding the appellant guilty of the deficiency in service and<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 06-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 3318/2023</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Case Partly allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('13','2026','2026_2_455_480','2026INSC135','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-